a_per_play":-0.00589,"pass_rate":0.7241,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5556,"def_epa_per_play":0.2078},{"week":8,"opponent":"PHI","home":true,"pf":27.0,"pa":10.0,"off_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":0.02313,"pass_rate":0.5345,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5682,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1905},{"week":9,"opponent":"LA","home":true,"pf":13.0,"pa":20.0,"off_snaps":57,"epa_per_play":-0.1773,"pass_rate":0.6667,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5909,"def_epa_per_play":0.001743}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"PHI","distance":0.4059,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Patullo"},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.5527,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.5955,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.6651,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Dave Canales"},{"season":2023,"team":"NYG","distance":0.7022,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.1642,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"DEN","distance":0.2265,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2025,"team":"ATL","distance":0.2576,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.281,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NE","distance":0.3147,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Commanders are 2-5-1 through week 9 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 202 to 172. The offense ranks 20th in EPA per play and the defense 20th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the 2nd lowest screen rate and the 3rd highest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Commanders offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd lowest screen rate and the 3rd lowest under center rate in the league. Jayden Daniels has run the passing game, with Stefon Diggs leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Commanders defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 5th, and its weakest has been success rate allowed, where it ranks 26th. Odafe Oweh leads the team with 4 sacks, and K'Lavon Chaisson has added 3.5, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have the 3rd highest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Commanders have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 84% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their secondary was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Jayden Daniels has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,250 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Stefon Diggs and Antonio Williams leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Jacory Croskey-Merritt and Rachaad White. On defense, Odafe Oweh leads the team with 4 sacks and Rasul Douglas has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"David Blough is calling the offense and Dan Quinn is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Eagles under Kevin Patullo and the 2022 Colts under Frank Reich. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Giants and the 2023 Broncos under Vance Joseph.","trends":"The offense went from 18th in EPA per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 26% to 20%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}